:name: E1M-X V2N (Renesas RZ/V2N) M33-SM smoke
:description: Boot a single headless Cortex-M33 (M33-SM) Zephyr slice, no hardware.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-sim headless boot. `tan renode` (tan-cli,
# python/tan/core/renode_plan.py -> build_renode_argv) injects `$elf` (the resolved
# zephyr.elf) and `$repl` (this platform descriptor) via
# `renode -e "$elf=@..."` BEFORE this script runs; the `?=` defaults
# only apply when still unset, so the wrapper's values win and the
# script also runs by hand from the SDK root:
#
#     renode metadata/renode/renesas_rzv2n.resc
#
# The M33-SM is HEADLESS in production -- no UART console (see the .repl
# header); the firmware's console lives in the `ram_console_buf` RAM
# ring.  The `--sim-mode` gateway generates its OWN boot .resc and
# streams that RAM console to a TCP socket; this file just boots.  NB
# the gateway is NOT ported yet (tan-cli#77) -- its Python helpers went
# with the west command in ADR-0020 Phase 4, so nothing in any repo
# generates that boot .resc today.
#
# The default $elf here (a plain hello-world build) still produces NO
# console output: it is a normal board build with sci0 left disabled,
# same as real hardware. The .repl now models sci0 (issue #1158) so a
# firmware built with tests/renode/v2n_m33_sci0_console.overlay + .conf
# DOES get a real, observable boot banner + app console under this same
# platform descriptor -- there is still no `showAnalyzer` call here
# because a Python peripheral doesn't implement IUART; its output goes
# to the Renode log instead (`sci0: sci0 TX: ...` lines), visible on
# stdout the same way `showAnalyzer` output is under `--console`. Use
# --sim-mode for the ram_console path instead if that's what you need.
#
# NOTE: this descriptor does NOT seed `cpu VectorTableOffset`, unlike
# alif_ensemble_e8.resc (#947).  `alif_ensemble_e8.repl` notes the RZ/V2N
# M33 needs its Secure VTOR seeded on Renode v1.16.x just as the M55 does,
# so the same guessed-offset failure is reachable here for a non-lowest-
# vaddr link shape -- but no V2N image of that shape has been run to
# confirm it, and this file feeds the REQUIRED `renode · V2N101
# --sim-mode socket contract` context, so the change must NOT be made
# blind -- that required job builds this descriptor but does not boot it
# (its e2e step is a no-op `echo`, tan-cli#77), so it gives no such cover.
# Tracked as #958; do not copy the AEN fix here without a real run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
$repl ?= @metadata/renode/renesas_rzv2n.repl
$elf  ?= @examples/peripheral-io/hello-world/build/m33_sm-zephyr/zephyr/zephyr.elf

mach create "v2n101"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

sysbus LoadELF $elf

start
